From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:49:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 212/342] NeoCam: fixes from the tests on the board

The window starts the camera in its own thread (it touched views from
the application's). The window never waits for the camera controller:
the node's callbacks lock the window, so quitting deadlocked; the
controller answers by messages. The still format menu's type is an
int32. Motion detection fits a gain and an offset of the whole picture
(the camera's exposure), treats big changes of all of it as the light's,
waits three seconds for the camera to settle and wants motion in two
analyses in a row: none for minutes of a still scene, a hand caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
